{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.LrCoefficientHecke","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.LrCoefficientHecke","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lr_coefficient_hecke_trivial_case","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lr_coefficient_hecke_trivial_case","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L99-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.partition_empty_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.partition_empty_size","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L95-L97","doc":"Empty partition has size 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lr_coefficient_hecke_non_negative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lr_coefficient_hecke_non_negative","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L78-L93","doc":"**Categorical content of `c^λ_{μν}` for the Wenzl branching**\n(statement-level, sorry-free conditional on the\n`LRCoefficientHecke` class).\n\nThe Hecke-deformed Littlewood-Richardson rule states that the\ncoefficient `coeff` defined by the class is the multiplicity of\n`V_λ` in `V_μ ⊠ V_ν` under the standard restriction\n`H_{n_1+n_2}(q) ↪ H_{n_1}(q) ⊗ H_{n_2}(q)` of the\nIwahori-Hecke algebras.\n\nSprint-2 follow-up will replace the conditional statement here\nwith the actual multiplicity statement once\n`prop:wenzl-branching-sub-lemma-2-1` Lean lands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.coeff_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.coeff_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Trivial case: multiplicity of V_μ in V_μ ⊠ V_() is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.zero_of_size_mismatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.zero_of_size_mismatch","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Vanishing when sizes are wrong: `|λ| ≠ |μ| + |ν|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.zero_of_not_contains","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.zero_of_not_contains","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Vanishing when `μ ⊄ λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.coeff","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The LR coefficient `c^λ_{μν}` for partitions of the\nappropriate sizes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LRCoefficientHecke","kind":"class","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L52-L76","doc":"**Littlewood-Richardson coefficient class** (§3b-cond hypothesis).\n\nAxiomatises `c^λ_{μν}` for partitions of the appropriate sizes\nas a non-negative integer that records the LR-tableau count.\nSprint-2 inhabitation uses Mathlib's symmetric-function library\nwhen it lands; until then this is a class hypothesis consumed by\nthe Wenzl branching theorems.\n\nAll three fields are sorry-free conditional on the standard\nLR theorem (Macdonald §I.9 / Ariki §6); QOU consumes the\ntheorem as a class hypothesis per AGENTS.md §3b-cond. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:lr-coefficient-hecke","label":"prop:lr-coefficient-hecke","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.contains","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.contains","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L46-L50","doc":"Diagram containment: `μ ⊆ λ` iff each row of `μ` fits inside the\ncorresponding row of `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.size","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L43-L44","doc":"The size `|λ| = Σ λ_i` of a partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Partition","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lr-coefficient-hecke.lean#L39-L41","doc":"Young partition as a weakly-decreasing list of positive naturals\n(with the convention that trailing zeros are dropped). ","signatureChunk":0}]}